>> title: Samosa
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: indian, potato, pastry, fried, starter
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: samosas, sambusa, singara, vegetable samosa, punjabi samosa
>> pairs-with: mint-chutney, papadom
>> servings: 12
>> time: 2 hr
>> step.1: rub the fat in, mix to a very stiff dough
>> step.2: rest 30 min under a cloth
>> step.3: fry 2 min, until the peas lose their raw green
>> step.4: crush in, off the heat
>> step.5: roll, halve, and fold into cones
>> step.6: fry 15 min at 300°F, until pale gold and blistered

Mix @all-purpose flour{2%cup}(260 g), @ajwain{1%tsp}(carom seeds, crushed in the palm) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} with @ghee{1/4%cup}(53 g) rubbed through to the texture of wet sand, then bring it together with @water{1/3%cup}(80 mL) into a dough much stiffer than a pastry.

Rest @&(~1)dough{} under a damp cloth ~rest{30%min}.

Fry @cumin seeds{2%tsp}, @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), @green chiles{2}(chopped fine) and @frozen peas{1%cup}(140 g) in @neutral oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a #skillet{} ~fry{2%min}.

Crush @boiled potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; boiled whole in their skins, peeled, cooled) into @&(~1)pea masala{} off the heat with @amchur{2%tsp}(dried mango powder), @garam masala{1%tsp}, @cilantro{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}, leaving it lumpy.

Roll @&(~3)rested dough{} in six balls into thin ovals, cut each in half across, brush the straight edge with @water{2%Tbs}, roll it into a cone, pack it with @&(~1)filling{} and pinch the top shut in a pleat.

Fry @&(~1)filled cones{} in @neutral oil{6%cup}(1.4 L) at 300°F (150°C) ~fry{15%min}, turning them, until they are pale gold and the surface has gone bubbled and blistered rather than smooth.

Low and slow is the whole trick, and it is the opposite of every other thing that goes in a fryer. Hot oil browns a samosa in four minutes and leaves the pastry raw and hard inside; fifteen minutes at 300°F is what gives the flaky, bubbled shell. There is nothing in the filling that needs cooking, so nothing is lost by taking the time. Keema samosas are the same cone with spiced lamb mince in them.
